age":19.8,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":1.344993839395725,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":59.0,"_gate_accruals":-0.09405396223312314,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":85.0,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.15911544893422938,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":68.8,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.04873705817608112,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":39.1,"_gate_piotroski":8,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":88.9,"_gate_spread":0.006121480099710558,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":3.1,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.30598011442226614,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":49.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.10387806473112902,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":51.3,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.07168462146784854,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":57.2,"_gate_pool_share":0.017811158059947818,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":47.1,"_gate_rev_durability":0.06689665792477317,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":58.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.00013406591750970975,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":49.9,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.010496617909105528,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":22.8,"_gate_share_shrink":0.0391691738216291,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":1.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.008988655095510521,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":85.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.01741,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":11.6,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"AZZ Inc. provides hot-dip galvanizing and coil coating solutions in North America. It operates through the AZZ Metal Coatings; and the AZZ Precoat Metals segments. The company offers metal coating solutions for corrosion protection, including hot-dip galvanizing, spin galvanizing, powder coating, anodizing, and plating to the steel fabrication and other industries. It also provides aesthetic and corrosion protective coatings and related value-added services for steel and aluminum coil primarily serving the construction; appliance; heating, ventilation, and air conditioning; container; transportation; and other end markets. AZZ Inc. was incorporated in 1956 and is headquartered in Fort Worth, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas E. Ferguson | President, CEO & Director | Age 69 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $438K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers, improving at 9%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $118K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["AZZ Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $3.8B market cap on $1.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 24% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $445M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 27 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.66\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -9.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 4.8\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.1183255519824059},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","16 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Industrials peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"AZZ Inc. Releases 2026 Sustainability Report","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/azz-inc-releases-2026-sustainability-report-302932408.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794000600.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Critical Review: Griffon (NYSE:GFF) & AZZ (NYSE:AZZ)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/critical-review-griffon-nysegff-azz-nyseazz.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793896134.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.914,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is AZZ (AZZ) Undervalued As Strong Quarterly Results Beat Expectations?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-azz/azz/news/is-azz-azz-undervalued-as-strong-quarterly-results-beat-expe","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793571814.005,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.854,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Should Earnings Beat Require Action From AZZ (AZZ) Investors?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-azz/azz/news/should-earnings-beat-require-action-from-azz-azz-investors","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793428981.329,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.791,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Understanding the Setup: (AZZ) and Scalable Risk","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/91/Understanding_the_Setup:_AZZ_and_Scalable_Risk_103126015802_1793426282.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793426282.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Here is What to Know Beyond Why AZZ Inc. (AZZ) is a Trending Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3019432/here-is-what-to-know-beyond-why-azz-inc-azz-is-a-trending-stock?ci